kit-forecast
============

kit-forecast is a Rust port of KiT ("KiT: A Foundation Model for Candlestick Time-Series
Forecasting via Diffusion Transformers"). It is NOT the official KiT implementation and is not
affiliated with or endorsed by the KiT authors.

Original work
-------------
  Project:     KiT
  Authors:     Boyu Zhang, Haorui Li (as named in the upstream citation block);
               repository commits are by "Boyu" (GitHub: Luciferbobo)
  Repository:  https://github.com/Luciferbobo/KiT
  Paper:       arXiv:2609.34507
  Licence:     "Released under the AGPL-3.0 license" (upstream README). The upstream LICENSE file
               is the unmodified GNU Affero General Public License, version 3. Upstream source
               files carry no copyright headers and no "only"/"or later" wording; the
               reference revision used for this port is 02a6887 (see README.md).

This port is derived from the upstream Python source (kit_v1/model, kit_v1/infer, kit_v1/data,
kit_v1/config.py and eval/infer_for_pred.py). The architecture, tensor layout, normalisation
constants, calendar rules, sampler and post-processing follow that source. Because the work is a
direct port, it is distributed under the same licence: GNU AGPL v3 (SPDX: AGPL-3.0-only).
The full text is in the LICENSE file.

Modifications
-------------
  * Rewritten from Python/PyTorch to Rust on the Candle tensor library.
  * Pickle/zip checkpoint reader written in Rust so the official .pt loads without Python.
  * PyTorch-compatible Mersenne-Twister/Box-Muller noise generator.
  * Typed high-level API (requests, options, results), structured errors, batching.
  * Input validation and typed calendars added; upstream training, plotting, backtest and
    metric code is not ported.
  * Test fixtures under tests/fixtures/tiny were generated with the upstream Python code from
    synthetic inputs and randomly initialised weights; they contain no upstream data.

Not covered by the software licence
-----------------------------------
The pretrained weights (Hugging Face: Lucifer744/KiT_model) and the demo dataset
(Hugging Face: Lucifer744/KiT_data_demo) are NOT part of this package. Neither Hugging Face
repository declares a licence in its metadata; both cards only say "See the main repository for
license information". The AGPL text in the code repository does not state that it extends to
model weights or data. This crate therefore ships no weights and no market data except
src/data/ashare_stats.json (35 normalisation constants, see below). Check with the KiT authors
before redistributing weights or data, or using them commercially.

src/data/ashare_stats.json is a verbatim copy of stats.json from the demo dataset: numeric
normalisation scales that the model requires to interpret its inputs and outputs.

Third-party dependencies are used under their own licences (MIT/Apache-2.0 and similar); see
Cargo.toml and `cargo tree`.
